1101
00:59:01,290 --> 00:59:03,600
We're sampling to
approximate our expectation

1102
00:59:03,600 --> 00:59:05,040
over all the stochasticity.

1103
00:59:05,040 --> 00:59:08,760
We're bootstrapping because we
don't want to use a full return.

1104
00:59:08,760 --> 00:59:12,510
We are, instead, taking
V to approximate that.

1105
00:59:12,510 --> 00:59:15,280
It can be used in episodic
or infinite horizon settings.

1106
00:59:15,280 --> 00:59:17,910
It is generally lower variance
