01:11:22,610 --> 01:11:24,485
And feel free to talk
to someone next to you.

1360
01:11:26,982 --> 01:11:28,690
And again, the intent
of this is to think

1361
01:11:28,690 --> 01:11:31,420
about, are these actually
computing the same thing

1362
01:11:31,420 --> 01:11:32,535
or not in this case.

1363
01:11:35,080 --> 01:11:36,910
And remember, this is
a different setting

1364
01:11:36,910 --> 01:11:39,160
than what I told you before,
that both of these things

1365
01:11:39,160 --> 01:11:40,610
can be consistent.

1366
01:11:40,610 --> 01:11:42,695
But that was if you
get infinite data.

1367
01:11:42,695 --> 01:11:44,320
What this is looking
at is, if you only

1368
01:11:44,320 --> 01:11:46,930
have a finite amount of
data, and you just go over it

1369
01:11:46,930 --> 01:11:50,050
over, and over again, either
with Monte Carlo updates

1370
01:11:50,050 --> 01:11:53,040
or with TD, will you
converge to the same thing.

1371
01:11:56,250 --> 01:11:58,000
And if you're not sure
or you're confused,

1372
01:11:58,000 --> 01:11:59,625
feel free to put that
