1435
01:17:18,220 --> 01:17:21,670
We, for Monte Carlo, we just
average over all the returns

1436
01:17:21,670 --> 01:17:23,030
we've seen where that.

1437
01:17:23,030 --> 01:17:24,110
So that's only 0.

1438
01:17:24,110 --> 01:17:28,030
So I bring this up because,
even though, asymptotically, all

1439
01:17:28,030 --> 01:17:30,010
of these things converge
to the right thing

1440
01:17:30,010 --> 01:17:32,822
under some mild assumptions,
with finite data, which

1441
01:17:32,822 --> 01:17:35,030
is what we're almost always
going to have in reality,

1442
01:17:35,030 --> 01:17:36,642
even if you go over
